From 58452c20ff9ab08c625756b8ccbd155242144d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UML Android <uml@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] um: virtio shared memory regions for vhost-user devices

virtio-gpu's host-visible memory (and other virtio shared memory regions)
are guest physical ranges whose contents live in the device backend. With
VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_SHMEM, virtio_uml asks the backend for the region
sizes (GET_SHMEM_CONFIG), reserves guest physical windows for them above RAM
(get_shm_region()), and maps the host files the backend passes with
SHMEM_MAP requests there, removing them on SHMEM_UNMAP.

- physmem.c keeps a registry of the mapped ranges: phys_mapping() resolves
  them, so userspace mappings of such pages map the backend's file directly
  in the stub, and the kernel keeps its own mapping for user copies.
- User copies (uaccess.c) use that mapping for pages outside RAM.
- The stubs' FD cache keeps only the RAM file: shared memory FDs are closed
  again and their numbers reused.
---
